    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d665">

                <pb facs="0522" n="514" sameAs="frus:frus1937v04/pg514"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">394.115 Panay/163: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Commander in Chief of the United States Asiatic
                        Fleet</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Yarnell</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Chief of Naval
                        Operations</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Leahy</hi>)<anchor n="93" xml:id="d665-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Shanghai</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-12-20T22:56:00+08:00">December 20, 1937—10:56
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received December 20—9:02 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>0120. At press conference by General Harada, Japanese Military Attaché, he said
                    that Japanese boat which bombed <hi rendition="#italic">Panay</hi> at 1100, 12
                    December gave warning that the vessel was in dangerous zone, that <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Panay</hi> fired at Japanese troops on shore with main
                    battery, and that the army boat which boarded the <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Panay</hi> before she sank did not machine-gun the vessel before boarding.
                    These statements are entirely contrary to all evidence given by survivors to
                    Court of Inquiry.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
